# Normalise line endings for everyone.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out
# as CRLF. Prettier is configured with `"endOfLine": "lf"`, so without this a
# fresh Windows clone fails `npm run format:check` on every tracked text file
# before the user has changed anything, and their first commit then has
# lint-staged rewrite each staged file to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The hooks are run by `sh`, which on Linux (`sh -e`, as husky's own runner
# uses) treats a trailing carriage return as part of the command and dies with
# `Missing script: "typecheck"`. Covered by the rule above, but kept explicit
# because it is the one place where CRLF is fatal rather than merely noisy.
.husky/** text eol=lf

# Screenshot baselines are binary: never touch them.
*.png -text
